                "text": "Let me understand the rule. Input grid is h\u00d7w. Output is 2h \u00d7 2w.\n\nx0 = vmirror(I) \u2014 horizontal flip (left-right mirror).\nx1 = hconcat(I, x0) \u2014 [I | mirrored horizontally] \u2192 h \u00d7 2w.\nx2 = hmirror(x1) \u2014 vertical flip (top-bottom mirror) \u2192 h \u00d7 2w.\nx3 = vconcat(x1, x2) \u2014 2h \u00d7 2w.\n\nSo output is the input plus its horizontal mirror on the right, and then the whole thing flipped vertically on the bottom.\n\nWait, x1 = [I | vmirror(I)]. x2 = hmirror(x1) = vertical flip of x1. x3 = x1 over x2.\n\nSo output top half is I followed by its left-right mirror. Bottom half is the vertical flip of the top half.\n\nActually since vmirror of I means reversing each row. hmirror reverses order of rows.\n\nLet me verify with the example.\n\nI =\n```\n3 0 0 0\n3 0 3 0\n0 3 3 3\n```\nx0 = vmirror(I) = reverse each row:\n```\n0 0 0 3\n0 3 0 3\n3 3 3 0\n```\nx1 = hconcat:\n```\n3 0 0 0 0 0 0 3\n3 0 3 0 0 3 0 3\n0 3 3 3 3 3 3 0\n```\nx2 = hmirror(x1) = reverse row order:\n```\n0 3 3 3 3 3 3 0\n3 0 3 0 0 3 0 3\n3 0 0 0 0 0 0 3\n```\nx3 = x1 + x2:\nmatches output. Good.\n\nNow I need to create 3 demonstration pairs. I'll pick inputs and let environment compute outputs.\n\nI should pick varied inputs to teach the rule. Let me create 3 different small grids.\n\nLet me create inputs with various sizes and colors.\n\nInput 1: 3x4 similar but different pattern.\nInput 2: 2x3 grid.\nInput 3: 4x2 or 3x3.\n\nLet me just submit three different inputs.\n\nLet me use colors and patterns that vary.\n\nInput A:\n```\n1 0 2\n0 2 0\n2 0 1\n```\n3x3.\n\nInput B:\n```\n0 4\n4 4\n0 0\n4 0\n```\n4x2.\n\nInput C:\n```\n5 0 0 5\n0 5 5 0\n```\n2x4.\n\nThese should be fine. Let me call show_transformed_input for each.\n\nActually the tool computes output via verifier. Good.\n\nLet me make the calls. I can do multiple in one block since independent.",
